# The arm64 forms the producer (`lir_body`) emits, one row per form name, with what
# the shared passes ask of a form: its operands (`r` general register, `x`
# floating-point/vector register, `i` immediate, `a` address, `m` memory cell),
# which source is tied to a dest (`^0`), the flags it reads and writes, and its cost class.
#
# This file is a BRIDGE, and the one place these facts live (`arm64.instr`
# keeps only what the pattern matcher reads). The name column is the producer's;
# the last column is LLVM's AArch64 opcode as the pin names it
# (`AArch64GenInstrInfo.inc`, checked by `tools/arm64/check_opcodes.py`), with
# `[A|B]` where one name is several opcodes (a load's destination width is in its
# operand, not its name). A name with an addressing-mode suffix (`LDRX.ui`, `.pre`,
# `.post`, `.ro21`, `.pg`, `.gotpg`, `.fi`) or atomic suffix (`CAS.3al`) is not
# LLVM's: it is renamed to LLVM's with the .td matcher step (arm64 moves to the
# pin's .td matcher after the main merge, spike row 9's successor), and this file
# is deleted when that matcher reads `AArch64InstrInfo.td`. A call, a tail call
# and the return carry a variable number of registers: no row.
#
# Read by `llrm_target::instr::parse_opcodes` with `dialect.toml`; `rows()` is
# generated from it by `build.rs`. Placeholders: `{g}` W/X at `g32,g64`; `{f}` and
# `{s}` H/S/D at `f16,f32,f64`; `{z}` B/H/W/X and `{zn}` 0..3 at `z8,z16,z32,z64`;
# `{a|b}` is one alternative per row, in step across the name and the last column.
#
# name  operation  shape  widths  cost  fixed  reads  writes  flags  llvm
# ---- integer arithmetic and logic
ADD{g}ri       binary   r/r,i,i      g32,g64  alu        -  -  -  -/-          ADD{g}ri
ADD{g}rs       binary   r/r,r,i,i    g32,g64  alu_shift  -  -  -  -/-          ADD{g}rs
ADD{g}rx       binary   r/r,r,i,i    g32,g64  alu_ext    -  -  -  -/-          ADD{g}rx
ADDS{g}ri      binary   r/r,i,i      g32,g64  alu        -  -  -  -/N,Z,C,V    ADDS{g}ri
ADDS{g}rs      binary   r/r,r,i,i    g32,g64  alu_shift  -  -  -  -/N,Z,C,V    ADDS{g}rs
ADDS{g}rx      binary   r/r,r,i,i    g32,g64  alu_ext    -  -  -  -/N,Z,C,V    ADDS{g}rx
ADC{g}r        binary   r/r,r        g32,g64  alu        -  -  -  C/-          ADC{g}r
ADCS{g}r       binary   r/r,r        g32,g64  alu        -  -  -  C/N,Z,C,V    ADCS{g}r
SBC{g}r        binary   r/r,r        g32,g64  alu        -  -  -  C/-          SBC{g}r
SBCS{g}r       binary   r/r,r        g32,g64  alu        -  -  -  C/N,Z,C,V    SBCS{g}r
SUB{g}ri       binary   r/r,i,i      g32,g64  alu        -  -  -  -/-          SUB{g}ri
SUB{g}rs       binary   r/r,r,i,i    g32,g64  alu_shift  -  -  -  -/-          SUB{g}rs
SUB{g}rx       binary   r/r,r,i,i    g32,g64  alu_ext    -  -  -  -/-          SUB{g}rx
SUBS{g}ri      binary   r/r,i,i      g32,g64  alu        -  -  -  -/N,Z,C,V    SUBS{g}ri
SUBS{g}rs      binary   r/r,r,i,i    g32,g64  alu_shift  -  -  -  -/N,Z,C,V    SUBS{g}rs
SUBS{g}rx      binary   r/r,r,i,i    g32,g64  alu_ext    -  -  -  -/N,Z,C,V    SUBS{g}rx
ADDXri.lo12    binary   r/r,a        g64      alu        -  -  -  -/-          ADDXri
AND{g}ri       binary   r/r,i        g32,g64  alu        -  -  -  -/-          AND{g}ri
AND{g}rs       binary   r/r,r,i,i    g32,g64  alu_shift  -  -  -  -/-          AND{g}rs
ANDS{g}ri      binary   r/r,i        g32,g64  alu        -  -  -  -/N,Z,C,V    ANDS{g}ri
ANDS{g}rs      binary   r/r,r,i,i    g32,g64  alu_shift  -  -  -  -/N,Z,C,V    ANDS{g}rs
BIC{g}rs       binary   r/r,r,i,i    g32,g64  alu_shift  -  -  -  -/-          BIC{g}rs
